from datetime import datetime
from typing import Literal

from .schema import QueryAnalysisResult


SchemaMode = Literal["none", "summary", "full"]


# ============================================================
# 1. 精简输出结构
# ============================================================

QUERY_ANALYSIS_SCHEMA_SUMMARY = r"""
Return ONE JSON object with all QueryAnalysisResult fields.

Top level:
schema_version="1.0";
status=success|needs_clarification|unsupported;
original_query:string;
query_type=BROAD_BY_DESCRIPTION|SPECIFIC_BY_TITLE|SPECIFIC_BY_NAME|SPECIFIC_BY_IDENTIFIER|BY_AUTHOR|METADATA_ONLY_NO_AUTHOR|UNKNOWN;
intent={task,mode,goal};
content:string;
constraints={hard:[],soft:[],exclude:[]};
relations:[];
logic={hard:null|LogicNode,soft:null|LogicNode,exclude:null|LogicNode};
properties={recent_first,recent_last,central_first,central_last,specific_paper_name,suitable_for_by_citing};
entities:[{type,canonical_name,aliases,source_text}];
domains={main_field,secondary_fields};
clarification={needed,unresolved_ambiguities,questions};
result_requirements={requested_top_k,required_fields,output_structure,need_relation_graph,need_open_access,need_code};
warnings:[].

intent.task=paper_search|paper_lookup|author_search|citation_search|literature_review
intent.mode=comprehensive|precise|latest|seminal|overview|specific
entity.type=topic|method|model|dataset|author|venue|paper|other
output_structure=list|table|relation_graph|mixed|unspecified

ConstraintItem={
 id:"C*/P*/E*",
 type:topic|task|method|technology|dataset|evaluation|author|venue|year|publication_type|min_citations|field_of_study|language|identifier|code_availability|data_availability|other,
 operator:eq|ne|gt|gte|lt|lte|any_of|all_of|contains|not_contains|between,
 value:scalar|null, values:[scalar], source_text:string, normalized_text:string|null
}

RelationConstraint={id:"R*",subject:string,predicate:string,object:string,level:hard|soft|exclude,source_text:string}

LogicNode:
LEAF={operator:"LEAF",ref_id:"ID",children:[]}
AND/OR={operator:"AND|OR",ref_id:null,children:[LogicNode,...]}
NOT={operator:"NOT",ref_id:null,children:[one LogicNode]}
"""


# ============================================================
# 2. 主查询理解 Prompt
# ============================================================

QUERY_ANALYSIS_SYSTEM_PROMPT_TEMPLATE = r"""
You analyze scholarly-paper queries. Convert the user's request into faithful
QueryAnalysisResult JSON for Retrieval Planner / Selector. Do not search,
generate retrieval queries, or invent requirements. Current year: __CURRENT_YEAR__.

RULES

1) CONTENT & CONSTRAINT LEVEL
- content = scientific meaning only; remove author/year/venue/result-format/link requests.
- hard = required or unqualified defining condition.
- soft = explicit preference: prefer/最好/优先/尽量/if possible.
- exclude = explicit negative: 不要/排除/exclude/without.
- Never promote soft to hard. Preserve source_text.
- Default hard logic is AND; default exclude means any match may exclude.
- Leave logic null unless explicit grouping/OR/NOT matters.

2) QUERY TYPE
SPECIFIC_BY_IDENTIFIER: DOI/arXiv/PMID/etc.
SPECIFIC_BY_TITLE: exact paper title.
SPECIFIC_BY_NAME: one specific resource by alias/name; merely mentioning a named method/model is insufficient.
BY_AUTHOR: papers written by specified author(s).
METADATA_ONLY_NO_AUTHOR: metadata constraints but no real topical content/author.
BROAD_BY_DESCRIPTION: normal topic/method/task/benchmark/citation-description search.
UNKNOWN: cannot reliably represent.
Priority: identifier > title > author > specific name > metadata-only > broad.

3) INTENT / PROPERTIES
task: paper_lookup(one exact paper), paper_search(matching papers),
author_search(author-centered), citation_search(citation relation central),
literature_review(explicit review/synthesis).
mode: specific, overview, latest, seminal, precise, comprehensive(default broad).

recent_first=true only for explicit recent/latest/newest/current.
"since 2023" alone does NOT imply recent_first.
recent_last only for earliest/older/foundational.
central_first for explicit classic/seminal/influential/highly-cited preference.
central_last only for explicit lesser-known/low-citation preference.
Opposite flags cannot both be true.
specific_paper_name = clear central named resource, else null.
suitable_for_by_citing=true only when citation expansion from a named resource naturally serves the request; otherwise false/null.

4) CONSTRAINTS
Use unique IDs: hard C1..., soft P1..., exclude E1....
Single-value operator -> value, values=[].
any_of/all_of/between -> value=null, values=[...]; between has exactly 2 endpoints.

Time:
"since 2023"/"2023年以来" => year gte 2023
"after 2023" => gt 2023; "before 2020" => lt 2020
"2020-2024" => between [2020,2024]; "in 2024" => eq 2024
recent/latest without explicit year => property only, never invent year.

Venue/year are separate metadata. Preserve paired alternatives when needed.
Author means papers written by that person; never infer coauthors.
Publication type only when explicit.
"at least 100 citations" => min_citations gte 100.
"prefer highly cited" => soft min_citations eq "high" + central_first=true.
Code/data availability is a constraint only when candidate papers must/prefer to have it;
requests for code/full-text/DOI links belong in result_requirements.

5) RELATIONS — IMPORTANT
Create a relation when the connection determines relevance, not merely keyword co-occurrence:
RL -> optimize -> LLM search agent
method -> applied_to -> task
model -> evaluated_on -> dataset
target paper -> cites/cited_by -> paper
method A -> compared_with -> method B
Level follows hard/soft/exclude. Do not split an essential relation into unrelated keywords.
Avoid duplicate hard constraints when a relation already expresses the same semantic requirement;
keep independent year/venue/dataset/evaluation constraints.

6) BOOLEAN LOGIC — IMPORTANT
Preserve explicit pairing. For:
"ACL 2024 or NeurIPS 2023"
represent:
OR(AND(venue=ACL,year=2024), AND(venue=NeurIPS,year=2023)).
NEVER flatten it to venue=[ACL,NeurIPS] AND year=[2023,2024].
Logic leaves reference existing constraint/relation IDs.

7) ENTITIES / DOMAIN / CLARIFICATION
Extract only useful entities; canonicalize/alias only with high confidence.
Never expand a broad concept into unmentioned specific methods.
Choose one broad main_field; add only materially relevant secondary fields; Unknown if unclear.
Prefer best-effort parsing. needs_clarification only when genuine ambiguity would materially
change retrieval and cannot be preserved safely; ask <=2 short questions.
Otherwise clarification.needed=false and questions=[].
Use warnings for non-blocking uncertainty.

8) RESULT REQUIREMENTS / STATUS
requested_top_k and required_fields only when explicitly requested.
need_relation_graph/open_access/code only when requested.
success=usable; needs_clarification=critical ambiguity; unsupported=no reasonable paper-search interpretation.

FINAL CHECK
Every condition/relation must be grounded in the query; soft stays soft; negatives, essential
relations and OR pairings are preserved; IDs are unique; logic references existing IDs;
do not invent authors, venues, datasets, methods or years. Return JSON only, no markdown/explanation.
"""


# ============================================================
# 3. 可选 Few-shot，默认不发送
# ============================================================

FEW_SHOT_EXAMPLES = r"""
Q: 找2023年以来使用强化学习优化LLM学术搜索Agent，并在真实科研查询数据集上验证的论文，最好来自ACL、NeurIPS。
